## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of Azure OpenAI deployment, API management, knowledge-grounding, data privacy, and governance in a realistic, beginner-friendly setting.

## Key Concepts
- Azure OpenAI Service integration with gateway
- Knowledge-grounding via Azure Cognitive Search
- PII redaction with Text Analytics
- Per-repo policy gating and audit logging to Data Lake

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: redactPII and gate before OpenAI call
function handleRequest(req){
  const redacted = redactPII(req.input);
  if (!policyAllows(req.repo, redacted)) return denyResponse();
  return callOpenAI({input:redacted});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate per-repo gating with mock sensitive files?
- How would you extend to support multiple KB sources and versioning nuances?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to architect a secure, scalable incident-response automation platform across tenants using Azure AI services. Covers real-time event ingestion, strict data isolation, guardrails for safe prompt generation, canary testing, and comprehensive audit logging.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time Event Hubs ingestion with tenant-scoped event routing
- Tenant-isolated Cognitive Search indexes for grounded KB retrieval
- PII redaction via Text Analytics before processing and storage
- Canary playbook execution behind API Management with traffic splitting policies
- Data Lake for raw audit logs, Cosmos DB for structured remediation results
- Azure AD RBAC for multi-tenant access control

## Code Example
```javascript
// Initialize per-tenant Cognitive Search client with Managed Identity
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require('@azure/identity');
const { SearchIndexClient } = require('@azure/search-documents');

async function getTenantSearchClient(tenantId) {
  const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
  const indexName = `kb-${tenantId}`;
  return new SearchIndexClient(
    `https://${process.env.SEARCH_SERVICE}.search.windows.net/`,
    indexName,
    credential
  );
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses practical Azure OpenAI engineering skills for data generation with governance, privacy, and observability.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant data policy gating
- PII redaction using Text Analytics
- Grounding with Cognitive Search and versioned KB
- Auditable logging to Data Lake

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example pseudo-code: gate -> redact -> search -> openai
function handleInput(input, tenant) {
  if (!policyAllows(tenant, input)) throw new Error('Not allowed');
  const redacted = redactPII(input);
  const kb = searchKB(redacted, tenant);
  return callOpenAI(redacted, kb);
}
```

